The '''2026 Vuelta a España''' is a three-week cycling race taking place in [[Monaco]], [[France]], [[Andorra]] and [[Spain]]. It started on 22 August in [[Monaco]] and will finish on 13 September in [[Granada]].<ref name="route">{{cite web|title=Official route of La Vuelta 2026|url=https://www.lavuelta.es/en/overall-route|website=lavuelta.es|date=17 December 2025|access-date=23 December 2025}}</ref> It is the 81st edition of the [[Vuelta a España]] and the third and final [[Grand Tour (cycling)|grand tour]] of the [[2026 in men's road cycling|2026 men's road cycling season]].

== Teams ==
{{Main|List of teams and cyclists in the 2026 Vuelta a España}}
Twenty-three teams are taking part in the race. All eighteen [[UCI WorldTeam|UCI WorldTeams]] were automatically invited. They were joined by five [[UCI ProSeries|UCI ProTeams]]; the three highest ranked UCI ProTeams in 2025 ({{UCI team code|TUD|2026}}, {{UCI team code|Q36|2026}} and {{UCI team code|COF men|2026}}), along with two other Spanish teams ({{UCI team code|BBH|2026}} and {{UCI team code|EKP|2026}}). The teams were announced on 30 January 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=LA VUELTA 26: TEAM SELECTION - La Vuelta 2026 |url=https://www.lavuelta.es/en/news/2026/la-vuelta-26-team-selection/51093 |access-date=2026-02-08 |website=www.lavuelta.es |language=en}}</ref>
