== Pre-race favourites ==
Five-time Tour de France champion [[Tadej Pogačar]] (UAE Team Emirates) arrived to the Vuelta regarded as the presumptive winner of the race, but retired from the race after crashing during the eighth stage. The Slovenian held a big lead in the race but got caught in a crash near the end of the stage. He tried to rejoin the race but was unable to due to severe injuries to his clavicle and spine, and was taken by ambulance to hospital. Race organizers confirmed he pulled out of the race.<ref>[https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/teams-riders/tadej-pogacar-abandons-the-vuelta-a-espana-after-crash-on-stage-8/ Cycling News report on Pogačar]</ref> Other contenders for the general classification include [[Felix Gall]] and [[Richard Carapaz]], as well as 4-time winner [[Primož Roglič]], despite having been hit by a car during training just 3 weeks before the start.<ref>https://www.cyclingstage.com/vuelta-2026-vuelta-2026-favourites/contenders-spain-2026/</ref> In the competition for the green jersey, [[Mads Pedersen]] and [[Wout van Aert]] were considered the favourites.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-08-22 |title=Five contenders for the points classification at the 2026 Vuelta a España |url=https://www.domestiquecycling.com/en/news/five-contenders-for-the-points-classification-at-the-2026-vuelta-a-espana/ |access-date=2026-08-30 |website=Domestique Cycling |language=en}}</ref>

